    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Facing a massive power deficit to overcome, the decisive crisis managers ordered an emergency load reduction. This courageous decision to prevent total collapse was taken to keep a critical 230-kilovolt transmission line from overloading, a direct response to an equipment failure that triggered the initial grid incident.",
      "source": {
